values ('sigiriya-and-dambulla', 'Sigiriya & Dambulla', 'Cultural Triangle', 'A fortress in the sky and a temple carved into rock', 'Climb the fifth-century rock citadel of Sigiriya and step into the painted cave temples of Dambulla, two UNESCO World Heritage Sites at the heart of the island.', array['Rising abruptly from the plains of the central dry zone, Sigiriya was transformed into a royal citadel by King Kashyapa in the late fifth century. A path climbs past landscaped water gardens, a gallery of painted frescoes and the polished Mirror Wall to the great Lion Gate, where only the carved paws remain, and finally to the palace ruins on the summit. Sigiriya was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1982.', 'Half an hour away, the Dambulla cave temple has been a place of Buddhist worship for more than two thousand years. Its five caves hold well over a hundred statues of the Buddha and ceilings densely painted with murals. The site was inscribed by UNESCO in 1991.', 'The surrounding countryside of reservoirs, paddy fields and forest makes this an easy base for Polonnaruwa, the medieval capital, and for elephant safaris in the nearby Minneriya and Kaudulla national parks.']::text[], '[{"title":"Sigiriya Rock Fortress","text":"An early start beats the heat and the crowds on the climb of roughly 1,200 steps to the summit."},{"title":"Dambulla Cave Temple","text":"Five painted caves filled with Buddha statues, reached by a short climb with views across the plains."},{"title":"Pidurangala at sunrise","text":"A neighbouring rock with a scramble to the top and a celebrated view of Sigiriya at first light."},{"title":"Elephants of Minneriya","text":"Late in the dry season, typically around July to October, elephants gather on the shores of the Minneriya reservoir."}]'::jsonb, 'Visitable year-round. Generally driest from around February to September; heavier showers are possible between October and January.', 'Around 4 to 5 hours by road from Bandaranaike International Airport, depending on traffic and stops.', array['culture', 'wildlife', 'nature']::public.interest[], 'sigiriyaAerial', array['sigiriyaRock', 'dambullaCave', 'minneriyaElephants']::text[], 7.957, 80.76, 0, true)
