values ('kandy', 'Kandy', 'Hill Country', 'The last royal capital, set around a lake', 'Sri Lanka''s cultural heart and home of the Temple of the Sacred Tooth Relic, framed by forested hills at the gateway to tea country.', array['Kandy was the capital of the last Sinhalese kingdom until 1815. At its centre stands the Temple of the Sacred Tooth Relic, Sri Dalada Maligawa, which enshrines a relic revered by Buddhists around the world. Daily rituals, accompanied by drumming, draw pilgrims and visitors alike. The Sacred City of Kandy was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1988.', 'A walk around Kandy Lake, created in the early nineteenth century, reveals the town at an unhurried pace, while the Royal Botanic Gardens at Peradeniya, a short drive away, are known for their orchid house and avenues of royal palms.', 'Each year, usually in July or August, the Esala Perahera fills the streets with dancers, drummers and caparisoned elephants over several nights. Exact dates follow the lunar calendar and accommodation is in high demand.']::text[], '[{"title":"Temple of the Sacred Tooth Relic","text":"Visit during an evening ritual to hear the drums and see offerings of flowers. Modest dress is required."},{"title":"Royal Botanic Gardens, Peradeniya","text":"Spacious, shaded gardens on a bend of the Mahaweli River, a short drive from town."},{"title":"Kandyan dance","text":"A cultural performance of traditional dance and drumming, often including fire walking."},{"title":"Esala Perahera","text":"One of Asia''s great processions, held over several nights, usually in July or August."}]'::jsonb, 'Pleasant year-round thanks to its altitude. January to April is typically the driest period; plan well ahead for Perahera season.', 'About 3 to 4 hours by road from the airport. Kandy is also on the main railway line from Colombo.', array['culture', 'nature']::public.interest[], 'kandyTemple', array['kandyPerahera', 'teaPlucking']::text[], 7.2936, 80.6413, 1, true)
