values ('south-coast', 'South Coast', 'South Coast', 'Palm-fringed bays, whales and slow days by the sea', 'From Mirissa''s crescent beach to the quiet sands of Tangalle, the southern coast is the place to unwind at the end of a journey.', array['The stretch of coast between Galle and Tangalle is lined with bays, headlands and fishing villages. Mirissa''s crescent beach is the liveliest, Weligama''s wide bay is known for beginner-friendly surf, and Tangalle offers long, quiet stretches of sand.', 'From roughly November to April, boats leave Mirissa harbour in search of whales and dolphins, including blue whales. Choosing an operator that follows responsible viewing guidelines matters, and sightings depend on the sea and the season.', 'Along the coast near Koggala and Ahangama you may see traditional stilt fishing. Today many of the stilt fishermen pose for photographs for a fee, but the practice remains a striking reminder of the coast''s fishing heritage.']::text[], '[{"title":"Whale watching from Mirissa","text":"Seasonal boat trips, typically between November and April, with responsible operators."},{"title":"Surfing at Weligama","text":"A gentle, sandy-bottomed bay well suited to first lessons."},{"title":"Quiet Tangalle","text":"Long, uncrowded beaches and secluded stays further east along the coast."},{"title":"Coastal food","text":"Fresh seafood, hoppers and rice and curry in small beachside restaurants."}]'::jsonb, 'December to April is generally the best season for calm seas and whale watching. The south-west monsoon brings rougher water from about May to September.', 'Mirissa is around 3 hours from the airport via the Southern Expressway, and about 45 minutes from Galle.', array['beach', 'wildlife', 'wellness', 'food']::public.interest[], 'mirissaBeach', array['mirissaShore', 'galleLighthouse']::text[], 5.948, 80.458, 5, true)
