values ('ancient-cities-of-the-cultural-triangle', 'Ancient Cities of the Cultural Triangle', 'culture', 'Royal citadels, sacred cave temples and medieval capitals, explored with a guide at an unhurried pace.', array['The Cultural Triangle holds several of Sri Lanka''s UNESCO World Heritage Sites within a few hours'' drive of each other: the rock fortress of Sigiriya, the cave temple of Dambulla, the medieval city of Polonnaruwa and the ancient sacred city of Anuradhapura.', 'We plan visits for the cooler hours of the day, allow time to linger, and pair the major sites with quieter places such as village walks and reservoir-side sunsets.']::text[], array['Early-morning climb of Sigiriya to avoid the midday heat', 'Guided visit to the painted caves of Dambulla', 'Cycling or driving among the ruins of Polonnaruwa', 'Time to rest between visits at a countryside hotel']::text[], array['Shoulders and knees should be covered at temples, and shoes and hats removed.', 'Sigiriya involves around 1,200 steps and some exposed stairways.', 'Site entrance fees are set by the authorities and may change.']::text[], '2–4 days', 'sigiriyaRock', 0, true)
