values ('tea-country-estates', 'Tea Country Estates', 'nature', 'Rolling estates, cool mountain air and a closer look at how Ceylon tea is grown, plucked and processed.', array['Tea has shaped the landscape and communities of Sri Lanka''s highlands since the nineteenth century. Around Nuwara Eliya, Talawakelle and Ella, estates cover the slopes in neat green terraces.', 'A visit to a working tea factory shows the journey from leaf to cup, and estate bungalows offer a peaceful place to stay among the plantations.']::text[], array['Tea factory visit and tasting', 'Walks through estate paths and viewpoints', 'Optional stay in a converted planter''s bungalow']::text[], array['Evenings in the highlands can be cool, so pack a warm layer.', 'Please ask before photographing tea pluckers at work.']::text[], '1–3 days', 'teaPlucking', 3, true)
